  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed in news reports and medical contexts. Often associated with heart-related conditions, overwork ({過労死|かろうし}), or hidden health problems. Can be used as a する verb: {急死|きゅうし}する (to die suddenly).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {急死|きゅうし}する (to die suddenly)\n- {突然|とつぜん}の{急死|きゅうし} (a sudden, unexpected death)\n- {心臓|しんぞう}{急死|きゅうし} (cardiac sudden death)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {突然死|とつぜんし}: sudden death — very similar; slightly more emphasis on the unexpectedness\n- {過労死|かろうし}: death from overwork — a specific cause of sudden death, well-known internationally",
